            <title>[LU-20560] checkpatch man4 nag fires regardless of documentation</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20560</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;tt&gt;LUSTRE_{RO,RW,WO&lt;/tt&gt;}_ATTR spelling.txt entries warn that a new sysfs parameter needs a Documentation/man4/ page, but fire on the macro token unconditionally — with CI gating on warnings, a patch adding a parameter fails whether or not the page exists, and additions to the spelling dictionaries trip their own entries. Suppress the warning when a matching man4 page exists and exempt the dictionaries from their own scan.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
